# Rust. Unanchored, so it catches `reference/rust/target/` too -- that is its
# own workspace with its own build directory, and `/target/` matched only the
# root one. 1,386 build artifacts were tracked before this was noticed.
target/
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.orig

# Python reference implementation
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/

# Logs produced by demos
*.jsonl
!conformance/*.json
# `*.json` above does not match `*.jsonl` -- this is the corpus
# `scripts/differential.sh` requires and was silently uncommitted for exactly
# that reason. Named explicitly rather than widened to `conformance/*.jsonl*`,
# so a scratch `.jsonl` dropped in `conformance/` during debugging stays
# ignored.
!conformance/adversarial.jsonl
# ...except the published one. A project whose whole claim is "anyone can
# re-derive every settled result from the log" has to ship a log. See
# launch/README.md and scripts/make-launch-log.sh.
!launch/cairn.jsonl

# macOS AppleDouble sidecars; this volume creates one per file
._*
.DS_Store

# Local node state: transport identity, ML-DSA root key, checkpoints, and log.
.local/

# The content-addressed cache of pinned verifier code. Every blob in it is
# recoverable from the pin in the objective that names it, so it is a cache and
# never a source: committing one would put a second copy of a checker in the
# repository, under a different path, that nothing checks against the first.
.cairn/
# The same directory under the name it had before the project was renamed.
# `BlobStore::under` and `ShardStore::under` still read it when `.cairn/` is
# absent, so a checkout that predates the rename keeps working -- and its
# contents must stay untracked either way: a blob cache is derived data.
.proofwork/

# Written by setup.sh / `make mcp` with absolute paths for one machine.
# Generated, not shared.
.mcp.json
opencode.json

# Bootstrap addresses are local configuration, never repository content.
# `cairn-p2p`'s own module doc says it: "Identity files and bootstrap files
# are local configuration. They are never placed in the append-only ledger."
# `.local/seed.json` above already covers the one `make p2p` generates; these
# catch a hand-written one beside it.
bootstrap.json
bootstrap.*.json

# The Next.js chain reader in ui/. Lockfile is committed (a UI built from an
# unpinned resolution is as unreproducible as a binary built from one); build
# output and dependencies are not.
ui/node_modules/
ui/.next/
ui/out/
ui/next-env.d.ts
ui/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# cairn-mcp's nonce sidecar (`<log>.pending.json`) holds unrevealed artifacts
# and the nonces that bind them; publishing one hands a copier everything it
# needs to front-run the commitment. Never tracked. Same for a server's stderr
# log, which carries whatever absolute paths the operator ran it from.
*.pending.json
*.log

# Crypto autoresearcher runtime state: the submitter identity (whose secret
# half IS the name, so a leak is impersonation and a loss is unrecoverable),
# the solver binary, generated artifacts, and the journal. The code it runs is
# tracked, under research/crypto-autoresearcher/.
.autoresearcher/
